    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d484">

                <pb facs="0675" n="595" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg595"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 Italy/289</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-06-03">June 3, 1936</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>At the President’s request, I submitted this draft reply to Rome<anchor n="49"
                        xml:id="d484-f1"/> to Secretary Morgenthau at the Treasury this afternoon.
                    We discussed the whole matter from various angles and Mr. Morgenthau agreed
                    entirely to the Department’s draft instructions. I thereupon called up the White
                    House and asked Mr. McIntyre to convey this message to the President inasmuch as
                    the latter had just left the offices. Mr. McIntyre promised to do so at
                    once.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
